---
title: "encode_account (Osaka Fork Types (ethereum/execution-specs))"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_compute_hash: code_hash = keccak256(raw_account_data.code)
    q_compute_hash --> q_build_tuple: tuple = (nonce, balance, storage_root, code_hash)
    q_build_tuple --> q_encode: encoded = rlp.encode(tuple)
    q_encode --> [*]: return encoded
    note right of q_encode
        INV-001: raw_account_data must be a valid Account instance with nonce, balance, and code fields
        INV-002: storage_root must be a 32-byte value representing the Merkle root of the account's storage trie
        INV-003: The RLP encoding order is strictly (nonce, balance, storage_root, keccak256(code))
    end note
